    "post_edition_date_source": false,
    "summary_or_snippet": "Israel kills three Palestinians in Gaza attacks Israeli attacks have killed at least three Palestinians in the Gaza Strip, including two people targeted by a drone in the north of the enclave. Palestinian health authorites said an Israeli drone struck the al-Salatin area, west of Beit Lahia, killing two people and wounding at least one more. In southern Gaza, Israeli forces also bombed a tent sheltering displaced Palestinians in Khan Younis. An Israeli warplane fired a missile at the tent, wounding several people who were taken to hospital for treatment. Medical staff at Nasser Medical Complex said they received the body of one unidentified person after the attack on the tent. Earlier, health officials in Gaza said Israel's war on the enclave had killed at least 73,054 Palestinians and wounded 173,480 since October 7, 2023. They added that hospitals had received three bodies and treated 43 wounded people over the past 24 hours.",
